      "title": "DM Draft: What Decides a Soul's Destination?",
      "type": "Plot",
      "categoryId": 2,
      "summary": "OPEN QUESTION — not decided yet. When a mortal dies, what sends their soul to Aethelis or to Khavora?",
      "body": "Status: undecided (raised Oct 24, 2026). This is a DM-only working draft — nothing here is canon until Jim picks one.\n\nThe three candidate answers:\n\n1. Belief — a soul goes to the realm its faith promised it. Strong for cultures with opposed religions (elves expecting Aethelis, orcs expecting Khavora), awkward for the faithless or the deceived.\n2. Nature — a soul goes where its own nature fits: ordered souls to Order, wild souls to Chaos, regardless of belief.\n3. Claimed — a shard claims the soul: patron gods, Time, or even the remains of the twins pull the dead toward their realm.\n\nWhatever is chosen has to respect the locked facts: there are only the two destinations ([[Aethelis, the Unchanging]] and [[Khavora, the Maelstrom Womb]]), and good/evil are mortal labels, not cosmic facts — see [[The Two Afterlives]].",
